# Persistent memory (phone / Cloud Agent)

The user works from a **phone**, not a desktop. Cloud Agents run in the cloud. Do not assume local terminals, npm installs, or `localhost` services.

## Memory layers (priority order)

1. **`memory/` (RavByte AMS)** — read `context-index.json` → `11-shawq-domain-map.md` → topic file. See `.cursor/rules/ams-memory.mdc`.
2. **`AGENTS.md`** — scope discipline, subsystem map, incident lessons.
3. **agentmemory MCP** — only when `AGENTMEMORY_URL` points at the Railway service (not localhost). Use `memory_smart_search` / `recall` for past sessions.

## Every session

1. **Recall first** — read `memory/11-shawq-domain-map.md` and `AGENTS.md` scope discipline before editing code.
2. **Remember by committing** — append lessons to `AGENTS.md` and update `memory/` after structural changes (`npm run memory:maintain`).
3. **Surgical changes** — follow Karpathy guidelines; one concern per PR.

## Do not (phone workflow)

- Ask the user to run `agentmemory` locally, `npm install -g`, or open `localhost:3111`.
- Cold-grep the repo for features already mapped in `memory/11-shawq-domain-map.md`.
- Rely on MCP if unreachable — fall back to `memory/` + `AGENTS.md`.

## Railway agentmemory setup

Operator one-time steps: `deploy/agentmemory/RAILWAY.md`. After deploy, set in Cursor MCP env:

- `AGENTMEMORY_URL` — `https://<service>.up.railway.app`
- `AGENTMEMORY_SECRET` — from Railway deploy logs

## Project facts (quick recall)

- Scope discipline: no bundled unrelated edits; see subsystem map in `AGENTS.md`.
- KPI all-time highs: strict beat for intraday; celebrate only on `strictBeat`; records scoped to `CAMPAIGN_LAUNCH_DATE` (`2026-06-03`).
- Reporting timezone: `Europe/Istanbul`.
- Production: https://shawq-ads-production.up.railway.app/
